Corrective commit for the AEOS implementation-audit FAIL on 80b4d13d (three High
B4 trust/deletion defects + two parser findings) and three rounds of AEOS
plan-review required changes. New commit — 80b4d13d is left intact.

The same-root rename/move no longer runs on the watchdog observer thread. on_moved
enqueues one governed 'moved' event (old + new rel_path); the readiness-gated,
symlink/identity-safe, transactional lineage move + destination re-extraction runs
in the drain, with bounded-backoff deferral for every recoverable condition so a
move is never terminally consumed while it could still succeed and the old row is
never superseded until the move is proven safe.

- PB-005: remove observer-thread apply_same_root_move; V127 rebuilds the events
  table (literal 'moved' type + dest_rel_path + next_attempt_at, parity-validated,
  preserves queued rows/ids); enqueue_event/claim_queued/defer_event add bounded
  backoff; drain 'moved' branch gates on safe_for_watcher_activation.
- PB-006: os.lstat (non-following) dest confirmation + symlink_escapes + pre/post
  transaction identity re-checks close the probe->mutate->index TOCTOU.
- PB-007: _invalidate_content_locked fully invalidates an overwritten destination
  (FTS row, text excerpt, chunks, content metadata cols, its own generated card);
  apply_confirmed_same_root_move returns a distinguishable result
  (move_applied/move_already_applied/source_missing/conflicting_successor).
- PB-008: parser RLIMIT_CPU derived from timeout_s (_cpu_limits).
- PB-009: SIGKILL -> parser_failed (ambiguous); SIGXCPU -> parser_resource_exceeded.

source_missing indexes the destination as an ordinary source (no invented
lineage); reindex failure is retryable; reindex exhaustion terminates as
error/dest_reindex_exhausted (never a false 'done'). Evidence:
docs/evidence/source-index-phase-b/05-corrective-audit-response.md. No push/PR.

